* Fri Sep 04 2026 RootGPT <166707820+RootGPT-YouTube@users.noreply.github.com> 1.2.0-1
- YouTube: import a hundred channels and you get a hundred avatars. Until now
  the backfill filled exactly one more per app start, so a large import left the
  Home grid mostly blank for weeks. Three separate faults were behind it: a
  request with no timeout could hang and freeze the whole queue; without a
  consent cookie YouTube answers a channel page with a redirect to its cookie
  interstitial, ~590 KB with no og: tags at all, so the avatar was silently lost
  while the request "succeeded"; and on Qt 5.6 aborting a reply leaves its HTTP
  channel dirty, so every later request on the same manager finished instantly
  with no data — which is why exactly as many avatars arrived as there were
  parallel requests. Each channel page is now fetched over a manager of its own
  and read as it streams, stopping at the avatar: ~270 KB instead of 2.4 MB.
  Measured on a POCO M4 Pro: 48 channels from scratch, all filled in under 30
  seconds with no retries.
- YouTube: a "Fetch N missing avatars" item in the pull-down menu, for the ones
  a failing channel page left behind, without waiting for the next app start.

* Thu Sep 03 2026 RootGPT <166707820+RootGPT-YouTube@users.noreply.github.com> 1.1.0-1
- YouTube: the video is throttled to the lowest quality while the app is in the
  background, and restored on return. Background playback kept Gecko decoding
  and compositing every frame at full resolution for nobody: measured on a POCO
  M4 Pro with the screen off, the GPU sat at ~70% and the phone drew ~2.8W —
  as much as with the screen on. Now it is ~18% and ~1.7W, a watt less, with
  the audio untouched.
- YouTube: recover from a frozen picture. The decoder can end up starved of
  graphic buffers at high resolution and every frame then arrives too late to
  be painted, so the picture freezes while the audio plays on — and it never
  recovers by itself. A watchdog now spots it (dropped frames keeping pace with
  decoded ones while the clock runs) and re-primes the pipeline with a seek,
  then a replay, then a step down in quality.
- Removed a quality probe that could never log anything: runJavaScript's return
  value does not reach its callback on this WebView.

* Fri Aug 21 2026 RootGPT <166707820+RootGPT-YouTube@users.noreply.github.com> 1.0.1-1
- YouTube: the quality cap is now 720p instead of 1080p. Pinning FHD made the
  older devices struggle (decode + scaling can't keep up, playback stutters),
  so 720p is the ceiling and the ladder steps down from there to whatever the
  video actually offers.

* Fri Jul 03 2026 RootGPT <166707820+RootGPT-YouTube@users.noreply.github.com> 0.9.4-1
- 0.9.4-beta.
- YouTube: in-app search for videos AND channels, still fully keyless (no API
  key, no login) — suggestions while typing, Everything/Videos/Channels filter,
